Subject: cmd/compile: inline the atomic operations on wasm with GOWASM=threads
Last-Update: 2026-10-04

The wasm backend had no atomic operations, so every call into
internal/runtime/atomic and sync/atomic stayed a call to an assembly
body, each with a frame, on the runtime's hottest paths. With
GOWASM=threads the atomic intrinsics are registered for wasm with the
builders the other 64-bit ports use, and the generic atomic ops lower
to the threads proposal's load, store, exchange, add, and, or and
compare-exchange instructions. A read-modify-write yields the old
value, so a sum or a comparison is rewritten in on the way out of the
tuple, as amd64 does. Address 0 does not trap in wasm, so each lowered
op first checks its address and raises the nil dereference panic the
compiler's own nil check raises; the ops therefore fault on nil as the
other ports' do, and the explicit checks before them can go. Without
the feature the calls stay, as a module for an engine without threads
cannot carry the instructions.

diff --git a/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/_gen/Wasm.rules b/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/_gen/Wasm.rules
index 6028152..319a168 100644
--- a/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/_gen/Wasm.rules
+++ b/src/cmd/compile/internal/ssa/_gen/Wasm.rules
@@ -268,6 +268,41 @@
 (Move [s] dst src mem) && logLargeCopy(v, s) =>
 	(LoweredMove [s] dst src mem)
 
+// Lowering atomics
+// Present only with GOWASM=threads, when the compiler inlines the
+// atomic operations: the threads proposal's instructions. A read-modify-write
+// returns the old value, so a sum or a comparison is rewritten in on the
+// way out of the tuple, as on amd64.
+(AtomicLoad8 ...) => (I64AtomicLoad8U ...)
+(AtomicLoad32 ...) => (I64AtomicLoad32U ...)
+(AtomicLoad64 ...) => (I64AtomicLoad ...)
+(AtomicLoadPtr ...) => (I64AtomicLoad ...)
+(AtomicStore8 ...) => (I64AtomicStore8 ...)
+(AtomicStore32 ...) => (I64AtomicStore32 ...)
+(AtomicStore64 ...) => (I64AtomicStore ...)
+(AtomicStorePtrNoWB ...) => (I64AtomicStore ...)
+(AtomicExchange8 ...) => (I64AtomicRmw8XchgU ...)
+(AtomicExchange32 ...) => (I64AtomicRmw32XchgU ...)
+(AtomicExchange64 ...) => (I64AtomicRmwXchg ...)
+(AtomicAdd32 ptr val mem) => (AddTupleFirst val (I64AtomicRmw32AddU ptr val mem))
+(AtomicAdd64 ptr val mem) => (AddTupleFirst val (I64AtomicRmwAdd ptr val mem))
+(Select0 <t> (AddTupleFirst val tuple)) => (I64Add val (Select0 <t> tuple))
+(Select1     (AddTupleFirst   _ tuple)) => (Select1 tuple)
+(AtomicCompareAndSwap32 ptr old new_ mem) => (EqTupleFirst32 old (I64AtomicRmw32CmpxchgU ptr old new_ mem))
+(AtomicCompareAndSwap64 ptr old new_ mem) => (EqTupleFirst64 old (I64AtomicRmwCmpxchg ptr old new_ mem))
+(Select0 <t> (EqTupleFirst32 old tuple)) => (I64Eq <t> (ZeroExt32to64 old) (Select0 <typ.UInt32> tuple))
+(Select1     (EqTupleFirst32   _ tuple)) => (Select1 tuple)
+(Select0 <t> (EqTupleFirst64 old tuple)) => (I64Eq <t> old (Select0 <typ.UInt64> tuple))
+(Select1     (EqTupleFirst64   _ tuple)) => (Select1 tuple)
+(AtomicAnd8  ptr val mem) => (Select1 (I64AtomicRmw8AndU  <types.NewTuple(typ.UInt8, types.TypeMem)> ptr val mem))
+(AtomicAnd32 ptr val mem) => (Select1 (I64AtomicRmw32AndU <types.NewTuple(typ.UInt32, types.TypeMem)> ptr val mem))
+(AtomicOr8   ptr val mem) => (Select1 (I64AtomicRmw8OrU   <types.NewTuple(typ.UInt8, types.TypeMem)> ptr val mem))
+(AtomicOr32  ptr val mem) => (Select1 (I64AtomicRmw32OrU  <types.NewTuple(typ.UInt32, types.TypeMem)> ptr val mem))
+(AtomicAnd32value ...) => (I64AtomicRmw32AndU ...)
+(AtomicAnd64value ...) => (I64AtomicRmwAnd ...)
+(AtomicOr32value  ...) => (I64AtomicRmw32OrU ...)
+(AtomicOr64value  ...) => (I64AtomicRmwOr ...)
+
 // Lowering Zero instructions
 (Zero [0] _ mem) => mem
 (Zero [1] destptr mem) => (I64Store8 destptr (I64Const [0]) mem)
